# Clone's "You may have this creature enter as a copy of any creature on the battlefield" is its own replacement effect
# (CR 614.1c). CR 614.12: which replacement effects apply to a permanent entering is judged on it as it would exist on the
# battlefield, "taking into account ... continuous effects that already exist and would apply to the permanent". Humility
# ("All creatures lose all abilities and have base power and toughness 1/1") would take Clone's abilities there, so Clone
# copies nothing and is asked nothing: it enters as Clone, a Shapeshifter with no abilities, base 1/1 under Humility, and
# lives. The Ornithopter it could have copied is the only other creature (the positive control of a copy:
# clone-enters-as-a-copy-of-an-ornithopter).

[Bot1 Deck]
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Plains
Humility
Clone
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

